id: pm-0k4o8t
title: "GH-792: fresh-clone health must not require ignored runtime and empty extension directories"
description: "pm init ignores search and locks, and extension storage may be absent until first install, yet default health reports all three as required. Align default health with reproducible clone state while preserving strict structural integrity and pending-merge diagnostics."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-28T11:30:00.319Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-28T16:31:03.357Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-28T16:28:02.857Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: A normal clone produced from pm init passes directory health without recreating ignored caches; history and schema remain fail-closed structural requirements; strict directory policy remains available; health remediation never loops through pm init; fresh-clone SDK and CLI regressions cover the distinction
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make default health portable across real Git clones without weakening material integrity
value: Agents can use health as a required CI context-integrity gate
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: fixed
expected_result: Fresh clones pass default health without materializing ignored runtime directories.
actual_result: "Clone-optional extensions, locks, and search no longer block default health; strict mode still reports them."
